sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task, DECISIONS R2-R4, agent-observer-swamp-acts; the new key is made on the Node and never leaves it. docs/reference/node-agent.md#agent-secret.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: orbit:node-agent-rekey
  autonumber
  %% lane OP icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant OP as Operator<br/>artisan on Gateway
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as Target Node<br/>reached over ssh
  OP->>GW: orbit:node-agent-rekey 12<br/>--attempt=1
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `php artisan orbit:node-agent-rekey 12 --attempt=1`
  %%> - syntax: `<node> [--attempt=N]`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - the Node id
  %%> - `--attempt` numbers the request; the same number returns the same task, a higher number asks for a new key again
  %%> When:
  %%> - the Gateway refuses the Node agent's reports because its key is missing or doesn't match the recorded verifier
  %%> - `node:converge` failed because the Node agent's key doesn't match
  %%> - a planned key rotation
  %%> Who can call it:
  %%> - an operator on the Gateway host; there is no `orbit` CLI or MCP command
  Note over GW: Validate, lock the Node<br/>task #5134 · Node 12
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - Node 12 is an active, managed Linux Node with stored SSH host keys
  %%> - no converge or rekey runs for Node 12; both use the same lock per Node
  %%> Result:
  %%> - task #5134 recorded with the full intent; no key or verifier in it
  %%> - the old verifier stays valid; nothing has happened on the Node yet
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-node-agent-rekey
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts one Swamp run on serve (Node 209)
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - Node 12's address and SSH host keys; the SSH identity comes from the `swamp` role
  %%> - the key path `/etc/orbit/agent/secret`
  GW-->>OP: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5134
  %%> What you get:
  %%> - the task number, at once
  %%> Next:
  %%> - follow the task with `orbit operation:show`
  SW->>N: Make a new agent key<br/>on the Node · keep the old one
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - creates 32 random bytes on Node 12 and writes them as 64 hex characters to `/etc/orbit/agent/secret`, `root:root`, mode `0600`
  %%> - keeps the old key as `secret.previous`, for a restore if a later step fails
  %%> - prints only the SHA-256 verifier of the new key
  %%> Never:
  %%> - the key leaves Node 12, enters the task, a log or the vault
  %%> How:
  %%> - a tracked script through `@swamp/ssh` from 209, with sudo
  SW->>N: Restart the Node agent<br/>@swamp/cfgmgmt/systemd restart
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - restarts `orbit-agent.service`
  %%> Why a restart:
  %%> - the agent reads its key only when it starts; a reload can't change it
  %%> Until the Gateway records the verifier:
  %%> - the Gateway refuses reports signed with the new key; the agent retries every few seconds
  SW->>N: Check the Node agent<br/>active · key matches verifier
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - checks that `orbit-agent` is active again
  %%> - checks that the key file's SHA-256 equals the returned verifier
  %%> - when both pass, removes `secret.previous`; if that removal fails, the file is harmless (`root:root`, mode `0600`) and the next rekey replaces it
  alt the agent runs with the new key
    N-->>SW: verifier, SHA-256 only
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the new key's verifier
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event · verifier
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event; Swamp never calls the Gateway
    Note over GW: Store the new verifier<br/>old key void · task succeeded
    %%> Result:
    %%> - Node 12's recorded verifier is the new one; the old key no longer works
    %%> - the Node agent's next report is accepted again
    %%> - task #5134 succeeds
  else a step fails
    N--xSW: exit ≠ 0
    %%> When:
    %%> - the key can't be written, or the agent doesn't come back up
    SW->>N: Restore the old key<br/>secret.previous · restart
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - puts the old key back and restarts the agent, so it matches the verifier the Gateway still has
    %%> Why a rollback here:
    %%> - otherwise the Node agent stays locked out until a rerun
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    %%> The Gateway reads:
    %%> - which step failed and its error code
    Note over GW: Keep the old verifier<br/>task failed · rerun is safe
    %%> Result:
    %%> - Node 12's verifier stays unchanged
    %%> - task #5134 fails
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - run the command again with `--attempt=2` after fixing the cause; it makes a fresh key
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    OP->>GW: operation:show #5134
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - asks for the task's status every 2 seconds until it has ended
    GW-->>OP: status + result
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the current status, and the result once the task has ended
  end
